  "question": {
    "text": "A ring of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>&nbsp;is uniformly charged with a linear charge density&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and kept on a rough horizontal surface with a friction coefficient of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>. A time-varying magnetic field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is applied in a circular region of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> perpendicular to the plane of the ring as shown in the figure. Find out the time when the ring just starts to rotate on the surface. (take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>125</mn></math> SI units)<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0059_8dcd457f0f75.jpg\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 235px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Induced electric field,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;r</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>d&#966;</mi><mi>dt</mi></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>&#960;a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;r</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br />Torque due to field about centre of ring,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#964;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>qE</mi><mo>)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;r</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>&#960;a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math><br />The ring starts rotating when,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#964;</mi></math> due to electric field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#964;</mi></math> due to friction.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#964;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>&#956;mg</mi></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math><br />Solving,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#956;mg</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>&#960;a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> ."
  }
